.TH BOOTSTRAP 1 "2026-08-31" "Mu2e Shift Scheduler v1.0.0" "Mu2e Shift Scheduler"
.SH NAME
bootstrap.sh \- first-time setup for the Mu2e Shift Scheduler
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./bootstrap.sh
[\fB\-\-admin\-password\fR \fIPASS\fR]
[\fB\-\-no\-server\fR]
[\fB\-\-no\-tests\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sets up the project from a fresh checkout: locates Python 3.10+, creates the
.I venv/
virtual environment, installs dependencies from
.I requirements-dev.txt
plus an editable install of the package (\fIpyproject.toml\fR), copies
.I .env.example
to
.I .env
if absent, runs the pytest suite, and starts the development server via
.BR start-mu2e-shift-scheduler (1).
Safe to run repeatedly. A PowerShell counterpart,
.IR bootstrap.ps1 ,
provides the same flow on Windows.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-admin\-password " PASS"
Seed the local admin account with this password
(or set \fBMU2E_INITIAL_ADMIN_PASSWORD\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-server
Set up the environment but do not start the server.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-tests
Skip running the test suite after setup.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
    ./bootstrap.sh --admin-password letmein
    ./bootstrap.sh --no-server --no-tests
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR start-mu2e-shift-scheduler (1),
.BR stop-mu2e-shift-scheduler (1),
.BR deploy-okd (1)
